<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Committee of Public Safety</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1793">1793</a>–<a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Committee of Public Safety was the executive body set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">French National Convention</a> in April 1793 to direct the war and suppress internal revolt. Dominated from July 1793 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilien-robespierre">Maximilien Robespierre</a> and his allies, it ran the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reign-of-terror">Reign of Terror</a>, in which thousands of suspected enemies of the Revolution were executed. Its power collapsed after Robespierre's fall in July 1794, and it was abolished in 1795.</p></div>
